  "uprn": "200003991344",
  "decision_date": "03/10/2008",
  "description": "Change of use of ground floor from retail to A3 restaurant, erection of first floor rear extension, erection of a third and part fourth floor, and conversion of the upper floors to nine flats.",
  "site_name": "101-103",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "11/06/2007",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": null,
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "03/10/2011",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - The restaurant use hereby permitted shall not open to customers outside the hours of 0800 to 2300.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Before the development is commenced details shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority for a scheme of acoustic insulation to ensure the maximum noise level to be permitted within dwellings with windows and doors shut and any other necessary means of ventilation provided shall not exceed the \"good\" limits contained in BS8233:1999. These being LAeq,16hour = 30 dB in living rooms, and a night(07:00 - 23:00) LAeq,8hour = 30 dB and LAFmax = 45 dB in bedrooms, and a night LAeq,1hour = 45 dB in Kitchens, Bathrooms and Utility Rooms \".  The agreed scheme shall be implemented prior to the completion of the development.\r\nReason:  To ensure satisfactory environmental conditions for the occupiers of the proposed building.",
    "Condition : 6 - The building shall be constructed and adapted so as to provide sound insulation against internally generated noise between the restaurant and the flats, and between the flats themselves, of not less than 30dB (A) with windows shut and other means of ventilation provided. The agreed scheme shall be implemented prior to the completion of the development.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - Before the development is commenced details of a scheme show how the windows and doors of the flats would be hermetically sealed, when closed, and how the rooms would be ventilated, shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented prior to the completion of the development.\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - Before the occupation of the restaurant use details of fume extraction equipment including details of sound attenuation for any necessary plant shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented prior to the completion of the development.\r\n",
    "Condition : 9 - Before the development is commenced details showing the provision to be made for disabled people to gain access to the A3 unit and the flats above shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented before the development hereby permitted is brought into use.\r\nReason: To ensure that there is satisfactory access for people with disabilities.",
    "Condition : 10 - Before the development is commenced details of bicycle storage shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented prior to the completion of the development.\r\n",
    "Condition : 11 - Before the development is commenced details of measures for the harvesting of rainwater, the minimisation of water run-off from the building and the conservation and re-use as appropriate of other water supplies in the building shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The agreed scheme shall be implemented prior to the completion of the development.\r\n",
    "Condition : 12 - With the appropriate safeguarding conditions the development would not result in harm to the appearance of the site or the wider area, would not cause harm to neighbours' living conditions, and would provide suitable living accommodation for the occupiers of the approved flats in accordance with adopted policies IMP.1.2 (The Re-use and Recycling of Urban Land), IMP.2.2 (Regeneration of Hounslow Town Centre), IMP.5.1 (High Quality Building and Urban Design), IMP.6.1 (Planning Obligations), ENV-B.1.1 (New Development), ENV-B.1.8 (Access and Facilities for people with Disabilities), ENV-B.1.9 (Safety and Security), H.1.1 (Location of New Housing Development), H.3.3 (The Use of Upper Floors Above Shops and in Town Centres), H.4.1 (Housing Standards and Guidelines), H.4.3 (Residential Mix), H.6.4 (Extensions and Alterations), S.1.1 (Main Shopping Areas), S.1.3 (Non-retail Uses in Secondary Frontages), S.4.1 (Environmental Improvements to Shopping Areas), S.4.2 (Shop Front Design), T.1.4 (Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities for Developments), and Supplementary Guidance of the of the Hounslow Unitary Development Plan."
  ],
